  "notes": "# DevClash 0.1.0-beta.6\n\nSecurity update for macOS, Windows and Linux.\n\n- Protect local usage and settings files with owner-only permissions on Unix systems, including existing files when accessed.\n- Reject symlink and hardlink targets before writing local data files.\n- Include the GLib security fix used by the Linux desktop dependency stack.\n- Preserve existing account sessions, preferences and cloud-sync consent during upgrades.\n\nCloud credits use automatic eligibility checks with no daily earning cap. Timely usage remains convertible; late uploads remain in full token history. Provider credentials stay on the device. The deployed API enforces this policy independently of the desktop update.\n\nThis remains a beta. Platform signing, installation and update evidence is recorded with the release artifacts.\n\nBuilt locally on native hosts. Source commit: 461655d285176a1b67effe2c5c3696463d95314c.\n\nRelease verification: all native builds, updater signatures, macOS notarization, and Windows Authenticode checks passed. Apple Silicon installation, login/settings preservation, and Windows installation/removal were checked. Full device coverage remains incomplete, including physical Intel Mac testing and fresh Linux installation/update cycles. This beta is published with the owner\u2019s explicit approval of those coverage exceptions.\n",
